.TH RFG 1 "2026" "rfg 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
rfg \- lead a multi-step refactor locally
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B rfg
[\fB--format\fR json] [\fB--root\fR DIR] [\fB--show-risk\fR] [\fB--max-chars\fR N] \fICOMMAND\fR
.SH OUTPUT BUDGETS
.TP
.B --show-risk
Include risk/format blocks in apply/next output. Default is slim.
.TP
.B --max-chars N
Cap agent-facing output (context, digest, export, impact). Default 2000,
hard cap 8000. Capped payloads carry truncated/chars/token_estimate.
.SH DESCRIPTION
Stores a versioned roadmap in
.PA .rfg/roadmap.yaml
and mutable state in
.PA .rfg/state.json .
Apply runs in a git worktree. Git is the transaction system.
.SH COMMANDS
init, status, plan, next, apply, verify, rollback, why, impact, index,
import-scip, mcp, edges, migrate, doctor, completion, man, version.
.SH EXIT CODES
0 ok, 2 verify fail, 3 dirty, 4 unsupported, 5 conflict.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B RFG_OFFLINE
If set, refuse optional network features (none are used by default).
.TP
.B RFG_TELEMETRY
Opt-in local telemetry log at .rfg/telemetry.log. Never sent.
.TP
.B RFG_VERIFY_TIMEOUT
Seconds per verify command (default 60).
.TP
.B .rfg/env
Optional KEY=VAL file merged into every verify environment (e.g. PATH
with user-local mvn/go/cargo). Supports $VAR expansion.
.SH PLAN FLAGS
.TP
.B plan --list
List all steps instead of only the next compact definition.
.TP
.B plan --extras FILE
Allowlist side artefacts (e.g. rfgfeedback.md) without polluting path[].
.SH SEE ALSO
docs/INTEGRATION.md
